==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-come again.ogg|a=AU}}

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|informal|by ellipsis}} {{non-gloss|A polite formula used when one has not heard or understood what has been said, or to indicate surprise.}}
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:say again}}
#* '''1955''', [[w:Rex Stout|Rex Stout]], "When a Man Murders...",<!--... in title--> in [[w:Three Witnesses (book)|''Three Witnesses'']], October 1994 [[w:Bantam Books|Bantam]] edition, {{ISBN|0553249592}}, page 120:
#*: "Who says he did?" / "Aubry." / "Yeah? A guy in for murder? '''Come again.'''" / "Glad to. Beebe says so too."
#* {{quote-av|en|year=1994|title={{w|Pulp Fiction (film)|Pulp Fiction}}|passage=Vincent: A "please" would be nice. / The Wolf: '''Come again?''' / Vincent: I said a "please" would be nice. / The Wolf: Get it straight, Buster. I'm not here to say "please". I'm here to tell you what to do.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} {{non-gloss|Used as a polite farewell to a visitor, inviting a return visit.}}

====Usage notes====
* As a farewell, mainly used in retail stores and service establishments such as hotels and restaurants.

